po"><country>CN</country> <doc-number>85106354</doc-number> <kind>A</kind> </document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-7262990-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>7262990</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1195832A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>BYD BATTERY CO LTD</name><address><country>CN</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>LV HAIGANG</name><address><country>CN</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>BYD BATTERY CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>LV, HAIGANG</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>LV HAIGANG</name><address><country>CN</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>LV, HAIGANG</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>The present invention relates to a high-temperature nickel-hydrogen battery and producing method thereof. High-temperature charge efficiency is greatly improved by adding 0.1-15 wt% of titanium element additive on the weight basis of nickel hydroxide contained in the positive materials into the active materials, and the charge efficiency at the temperature more than 50  DEG C is up to 95 %. The nickel-hydrogen battery according to the present invention can be used at the temperature of 50  DEG C or above.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une batterie nickel-hydrogène haute température et son procédé de fabrication. Grâce à l'ajout d'un élément titane compris entre 0,1 et 15 % en poids du nickel hydroxyde contenu dans les matières positives, l'efficacité de charge haute température est considérablement améliorée. Ainsi, l'efficacité de charge à une température dépassant 50  DEG C peut atteindre jusqu'à 95 %. La batterie nickel-hydrogène peut être utilisée à des températures de 50  DEG C ou pus.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>